From fd2e65ca3193d07f546930369df2ec83fece2aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jdistler <josephcd921@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:52:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] demux: cap avdiff tape-delay compensation to a plausible
 60s window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0022 fired on abs(first-audio-video PES PTS diff) >= 3s with no upper
bound, so a coarse PTS-base mismatch triggered a bogus multi-second audio_delay.
panelfuzz wild-campaign 2026-07-12: fullent's 24/7 loop channels (The Rifleman,
Sesame Street) stamp video and audio in eras ~105s apart though the content
plays together; es_out.c set audio_delay=+105s, which would delay audio past
its own span into silence. A broadcast compliance buffer (the real tape-delay,
MLB +36s) is seconds to tens of seconds; >60s is a labeling artifact. Both
0022 sites (es_out.c raw TS + FakeESOut.cpp adaptive HLS) now gate 3s<=|diff|<=60s
— above the cap: no correction, no marker (the app pill must not mount a 100s
countdown), let the monotonic clock play the co-arriving frames together.

Verified: The Rifleman (-105s) no longer fires; MLB (+36s) still fires + compensates.

skywave-audio-tolerance branch.
---
 modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp |  7 ++++++-
 src/input/es_out.c                            | 13 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
index a794097bef..ac9c854fd0 100644
--- a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
@@ -731,7 +731,12 @@ int FakeESOut::esOutSend(es_out_id_t *p_es, block_t *p_block)
         {
             const vlc_tick_t diff = sk_first_audio_pts - sk_first_video_pts;
             const vlc_tick_t abs_diff = diff < 0 ? -diff : diff;
-            if( abs_diff >= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(3) )
+            /* Same plausible-tape-delay window as the es_out.c peer: 3-60 s.
+             * Beyond 60 s is a coarse PTS-base mismatch (loop channels), not a
+             * real delay — the app pill must not mount a 100 s countdown for it,
+             * so don't even fire the marker there. */
+            if( abs_diff >= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(3)
+             && abs_diff <= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(60) )
             {
                 if( sk_log_obj )
                     msg_Warn( sk_log_obj,
diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
index 7736e49840..6f8c49dbf0 100644
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -3210,7 +3210,18 @@ static int EsOutSend(es_out_t *out, es_out_id_t *es, block_t *p_block )
             const vlc_tick_t diff = p_sys->skywave_first_audio_pts
                                   - p_sys->skywave_first_video_pts;
             const vlc_tick_t abs_diff = diff < 0 ? -diff : diff;
-            if( abs_diff >= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(3) )
+            /* Compensate only within a plausible tape-delay window. A broadcast
+             * compliance buffer is seconds to a few tens of seconds (MLB Network
+             * +36s); anything past ~60s is NOT a temporal offset but a coarse
+             * PTS-BASE mismatch — e.g. fullent's 24/7 loop channels (The
+             * Rifleman, Sesame Street) stamp video and audio in eras ~105s
+             * apart though the content plays together (panelfuzz campaign,
+             * 2026-07-12). Applying a 105s audio_delay there would ACTIVELY
+             * break sync (delay audio past its own span into silence). Above
+             * the cap we do nothing and let the monotonic clock play the
+             * co-arriving frames together, which is already correct. */
+            if( abs_diff >= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(3)
+             && abs_diff <= VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(60) )
             {
                 msg_Warn( p_input,
                     "skywave-avdiff-large: first audio-video PES PTS diff "
